    "experiments": [
        {
            "number": 7,
            "title": "CMOS Inverter Design & Analysis",
            "date": "01/10/2026",
            "sections": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 1,
                    "title": "AIM",
                    "text": [
                        "To design an CMOS inverter repeater using minimum channel length and minimum width in 180nm technology and determine",
                        "1] $R_{out}$ , (output resistance of the inverter)",
                        "2] $C_{out}$ , (output capacitance of the inverter)",
                        "3] intrinsic delay $t_{p}$ , (intrinsic delay of the inverter)",
                        "4] $R_n$ , $R_p$ (resistance of NMOS and PMOS)",
                        "5] k (number of stage of repeaters)",
                        "to calculate propagation delay without inverter/buffer insertion and with inverter/buffer insertion and to compare the results."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 2,
                    "title": "TOOL",
                    "text": "Cadence Virtuoso"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 3,
                    "title": "THEORY",
                    "text": [
                        "1. Unbuffered Interconnect Delay: A long interconnect exhibits distributed resistance $R_{int}$ and capacitance $C_{int}$, causing propagation delay to scale quadratically with wire length. Driven by a minimum-sized inverter ($R_{out}, C_{out}$), the total unbuffered delay is given by $T_{50\\%} = 0.7 R_{out}(C_{int} + C_{out}) + R_{int}(0.4 C_{int} + 0.7 C_{out})$.",
                        "2. Minimum-Sized Repeater Insertion: Inserting intermediate minimum-sized inverters divides the line into $k$ shorter sections, converting quadratic delay growth into a linear relationship. The total propagation delay for $k$ minimum-sized repeater stages is given by $T_{50\\%} = k\\left[0.7 R_{out}\\left(\\frac{C_{int}}{k} + C_{out}\\right) + \\frac{R_{int}}{k}\\left(0.4\\frac{C_{int}}{k} + 0.7 C_{out}\\right)\\right]$.",
                        "3. Optimum Number of Stages: Minimizing the total propagation delay with respect to $k$ yields the optimum number of repeater stages: $k = \\sqrt{\\frac{0.4 R_{int} C_{int}}{0.7 R_{out} C_{out}}}$."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "number": 4,
                    "new_page": true,
                    "title": "Tables",
                    "tables": [
                        {
                            "title": "Design Parameters",
                            "csv": "param.csv"
                        },
                        {
                            "title": "Derived and observed intrinsic parameters",
                            "csv": "param_derived.csv"
                        },
                        {
                            "title": "Result",
                            "csv": "result.csv"
                        },
                        {
                            "title": "comparison of theoretical and practical values",
                            "csv": "the_vs_prac.csv"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "calculation",
                    "number": 5,
                    "title": "CALCULATION",
                    "new_page": false,
                    "variables": {
                        "k_n": 70,
                        "k_p": 20,
                        "R_int": 68,
                        "C_int": 60,
                        "V_dd": 1.8,
                        "V_tn": 0.45,
                        "V_tp": 0.45,
                        "W": 400,
                        "L": 180,
                        "t_phl": 9.8587,
                        "t_plh": 27.33919,
                        "t_phl_no_rep": 2.882,
                        "t_plh_no_rep": 3.119,
                        "t_phl_rep": 1.17325,
                        "t_plh_rep": 1.23534
                    },
                    "items": [
                        "R_n = 1000/(k_n*(W/L)*(V_dd-V_tn)) | unit: kΩ | round: 3",
                        "R_p = 1000/(k_p*(W/L)*(V_dd-V_tp)) | unit: kΩ | round: 2",
                        "R_{out} = (R_n + R_p)/2 | unit: kΩ | round: 3",
                        "C_{out1} = t_phl/(0.69*R_n) | unit: fF | round: 3",
                        "C_{out2} = t_plh/(0.69*R_p) | unit: fF | round: 4",
                        "C_{out} = max(C_{out1}, C_{out2}) | unit: fF | round: 3",
                        "t_{p(min)} = (t_phl + t_plh)/2 | unit: ps | round: 4",
                        "k = sqrt((R_int*C_int*0.4)/(R_{out}*C_{out}*0.7)) | round_down: 0",
                        "T_{p(no_rep)(theoratical)} = (0.7*R_{out}*(C_int+C_{out}) + R_int*(0.4*C_int+0.7*C_{out}))/1000 | unit: ns | round: 4",
                        "T_{p(rep)(theoratical)} = (k*(0.7*R_{out}*(C_int/k + C_{out}) + (R_int/k)*(0.4*C_int/k + 0.7*C_{out})))/1000 | unit: ns | round: 4",
                        "t_{HL(no_rep)} = t_phl_no_rep | unit: ns | round: 3",
                        "t_{LH(no_rep)} = t_plh_no_rep | unit: ns | round: 3",
                        "t_{p(no_rep)} = (t_phl_no_rep + t_plh_no_rep)/2 | unit: ns | round: 4",
                        "t_{HL(rep)} = t_phl_rep | unit: ns | round: 5",
                        "t_{LH(rep)} = t_plh_rep | unit: ns | round: 5",
                        "t_{p(rep)} = (t_phl_rep + t_plh_rep)/2 | unit: ns | round: 4"
                    ]
                },
