                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 7,
                    "title": "CONCLUSION",
                    "text": [
                        "1. An unbuffered interconnect and minimum-sized CMOS inverter repeaters were designed and simulated in 180 nm technology ($V_{DD} = 1.8\\text{ V}$, $R_{int} = 68\\text{ k}\\Omega$, $C_{int} = 60\\text{ fF}$).",
                        "2. Minimum-sized repeater insertion ($k = 8$) reduced propagation delay from $3.0005\\text{ ns}$ down to $1.2043\\text{ ns}$ (59.86% reduction), in good agreement with the theoretical delay of $0.9768\\text{ ns}$."
                    ]
